# GPU work stays on this PC (5060 Ti)

This developer machine has an **NVIDIA RTX 5060 Ti**. Any feature that needs GPU inference or heavy local ML must be developed, run, and validated **on this machine**, not assumed to run only on ECS/cloud.

## Typical GPU-bound work

- Whisper / WhisperX / faster-whisper ASR
- Local TTS / voice cloning / stem separation (Demucs/UVR)
- LiveTalking / digital-human avatar GPU services
- Local LLM inference used by oral coach / writing grade when not using cloud API keys
- Other CUDA / TensorRT / ONNX-GPU pipelines

## Rules of engagement

1. **Develop locally first**: install deps, download models, and prove the pipeline on this PC before documenting ECS deploy steps.
2. **Do not** require the Guangzhou ECS API box to have a 5060 Ti for day-to-day coding of these features.
3. ECS may still **call** a GPU service over Tailscale/LAN if one is exposed from this PC (or a dedicated GPU host); keep that as an optional remote endpoint (`WHISPER_*` / oral_coach provider URLs), not as “must train/run models on ECS”.
4. Mobile APK must never ship large GPU models; App continues to use cloud/API or on-device `whisper.cpp` where already designed.
5. When choosing providers, prefer: local GPU mock→real on this PC → optional cloud API fallback → ECS only for orchestration/storage.

## When the agent starts GPU-related tasks

- Check local CUDA / Python venv / model paths on this Windows host.
- Run smoke tests here (CLI or `tools/*/app`) before changing production ECS only.
- Say clearly if a step needs the user to start a local GPU service (port, env vars).
